From a7ae7bcf08225d3eed31f93faeee93f2b17d3b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:25:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] freetype: only use CoreText fallback fonts that
 FreeType can render

On iOS 27, CoreText picks PingFang for Chinese characters and
for most kanji, but PingFang only has 'hvgl' outlines, which FreeType
can not read, so those characters were not rendered. When the font
CoreText suggests has no outlines FreeType supports, look for another
font with the codepoint in the cascade list, and then among all fonts,
which includes the fonts activated by the application.

Keep the fallbacks found in a list per family, like on Windows, instead
of returning the family from the master list, whose other families
SearchFallbacks() walked through, which made the result depend on the
order the families were loaded. Also remember the codepoints without
any font, since searching all fonts for each of them is slow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
